# Other
curriculum/

# The RAG index and its metadata sidecar. rag.py puts these *beside* the
# corpus rather than inside it on purpose — is_index_stale walks the corpus
# tree, so an index stored within it would be newer than itself and stale on
# every check. That places them outside the curriculum/ rule above, so running
# a single chat left two untracked files in git status permanently.
*.faiss
*_docs.json

# Byte-compiled / cached files
*.pyc
*$py.class
